      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TOP PICK (4) gets the nod second-up after a fair fourth at Canberra, where she was beaten three and a half lengths and started near the top of betting. She just peaked on the run fresh, but showed enough to suggest a win is near. With natural progression, she can get the job done this time. SLATER'S BOY (1) is the immediate danger after beating TOP PICK home at Canberra, finishing third behind Hellfire Henry. That looks a key formline for this and now Loy rides. Leading chance. INSPIRITU (2) was beaten a head at Orange before a bumped-start fourth at Wagga, and third-up fitness keeps her right in the discussion. REINCZECH (3) resumes here after showing some positive signs in her debut campaign. Boudvillain riding is a big tick and she can resume on a positive note. AQUILINO (5) is on the quick turnaround and has claims on the back of a solid performance most recently.",
